{"term":"in spite of","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:4e3b36a90ea0a44e35","definition":"Despite, irrespective of, notwithstanding.","example":"No evening I had passed at Bly had the portentous quality of this one; in spite of which—and in spite also of the deeper depths of consternation that had opened beneath my feet—there was literally, in the ebbing actual, an extraordinarily sweet sadness.","pos":"prep","synonyms":["maugre","regardless of","despite","with","for all","irrespective of","maugre","notwithstanding","regardless of","in spite of","without considering","without regard for"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"idiomatic","register":"idiomatic","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/in_spite_of#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"us":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/e/e0/En-au-in_spite_of.ogg/En-au-in_spite_of.ogg.mp3"},"wordFamily":[]}